WEBVTT

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.100
My name is Taniyama Mai.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.940
I'm a first-year high school student with a
passion for supernatural and horror stories.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.530
One day after school, I was in the audiovisual room

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.990
with my classmates Keiko and Michiru,

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.590
telling each other ghost stories as usual.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.540
When <i>he</i> came in. Shibuya Kazuya!

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.290
He's stubborn, and bossy, and a terrible narcissist to boot.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:31.260
And get this: He's a professional ghost hunter!

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.680
There's a rumour that our old school
building is haunted by spirits,

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.800
so he came to investigate.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.390
But it wasn't just him.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:44.190
There was also a priestess, a monk,
an exorcist and even a medium.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.190
Are the ghosts here really that powerful?

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.110
As if that wasn't bad enough, Kuroda-san, a classmate
of mine who can apparently sense spirits,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:56.360
said that those spirits gathered here because
we were telling ghost stories!

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.200
If that's really true,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.620
what am I to do?

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:37.970
Filled with Evil Spirits?! Part 2

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.930
I perform this ritual to beseech the gods.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.980
I call upon them to descend from Heaven
to this place where no gods dwell,

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.110
to purify and end this ceaseless suffering.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:59.030
Please accept our plea for peace and tranquility.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.490
What's she saying?

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.270
Don't you know of Shinto prayers?

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:05.200
Shinto prayers?

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.290
Sort of like Shinto blessings.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.370
But will it really work?

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.920
I've never seen a Shinto exorcism before.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:17.760
Let's watch.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:24.720
Let this place be as the High Heavenly Plain.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.560
Gather here, all ye gods!

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.230
Hail Marishi-Ten, goddess of light!

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.020
Grant us protection and light in this school.

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.280
Now you'll have nothing to worry about.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.410
Oh, that was simply splendid!

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:47.370
It's fitting to have such a solemn ritual.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:49.870
What do you say?

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.660
We're going out to celebrate...

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.000
But once the exorcism has started, I like
to stay overnight to watch over things.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.250
I see. That's very professional of you.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.340
Well then, we should at least have lunch somewhere.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.390
Ah, it's finally over!

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.110
Hey, are you all right?

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.660
He's bleedin'!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.740
Him as well. Are they hurt badly?

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.230
Are you all right?

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:30.870
Yes, I'm fine.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.000
It's terrible.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:32.780
Yes...

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.170
Wh-What...

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:35.620
was that?

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:46.010
What do you mean, "Nothing to worry about"?

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:47.800
You can't even perform an exorcism.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.760
You even got the principal injured.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.890
That was an accident.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.350
That's right. Actually, I-

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:58.980
I did not mean that your exorcism worked.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.690
There were no spirits in the first place.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:03.490
There were!

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.650
Because something attacked me.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.450
Could it be a coincidence?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:13.700
There really is something here too strong for our priestess.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.790
If so, my instruments should have
registered something stronger.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.250
If only I had spiritual powers too...

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.880
I wish I could do something about the ghosts I summoned.

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:28.800
Eh?

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.640
There wasn't a chair in the middle of this classroom before.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:35.810
It's the east classroom on the second floor.

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:37.270
Yeah.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.020
It wasn't there when I put the camera there yesterday.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.980
I remember, I swear.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.400
Did anyone go into that classroom today?

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:47.570
Nope.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:48.990
Me neither.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.080
"Well then, we should at least have lunch somewhere."

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:12.050
What does it mean?

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.470
It may be a poltergeist.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:16.270
Poltergeist?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:20.270
It's German. I think it means "restless spirit".

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.980
They move things around and make noises.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.610
You're well informed, but I disagree.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:33.240
Things moved by poltergeists are warm to the touch.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.750
That chair isn't radiating any more heat.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.420
But based on Tizzana's criteria...

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.130
Tizzana?

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:43.750
E. Tizzana.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:48.340
He was a French police officer who made
a classification for poltergeists.

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:54.050
There are nine criteria which include objects vibrating,
doors opening and closing, noises, and knocking.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:58.980
If you look at all the phenomena that
occurred in this old school building:

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.020
Doors have closed, objects moved,

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.440
and glass broken. In total, three items.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.900
Then what about Kuroda-san being attacked?

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.780
She was simply imagining it.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.810
Just accept it!

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:15.450
There's a malevolent spirit here!

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.580
I'll look inside again.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.830
If there is a spirit, I should be able to feel it.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:29.630
If there really is a spirit and Hara-san doesn't feel it,

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.680
it'd be quite a shock.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.340
There's no proof that there is though.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.220
He's covering for her.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.420
Maybe Naru-chan's just going for looks.

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.980
Shibuya-san, you like pretty girls?

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.850
You seem to be covering for her quite a lot.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:47.320
God! And just when I was about to say it!

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.280
I know of her work.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.610
And I respect her talent very much.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.020
I'm simply giving her the credit she deserves.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.950
Then I wish you would give me more credit.

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:04.170
What about you should I compliment, Matsuzaki-san?

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.090
What was that?!

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:11.380
Ghostly sounds?

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:13.630
Those are made by ghosts?

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.140
Hara-san fell from that classroom!

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.520
The damage to the unrepaired wall on the east side

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:31.280
was covered with low quality plywood.

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:34.700
She happened to lean against it, and it broke under her weight.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.780
Hara-san said it was an accident.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:41.290
This was an accident.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.540
There was no spirit there, as I thought.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.170
I can't deny it any longer.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.040
There's an evil spirit here.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.840
Yeah, the one you couldn't exorcise.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.130
That thing is dangerous.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:57.050
A ghost left unexorcised is like a wounded bear.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:00.560
Then Masako's injuries were the priestess' fault!

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:01.390
What do you mean?

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.560
Don't jump to conclusions.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.980
From what I saw on the video, that was an accident.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:10.190
You say it's a curse because it happens over and over, right?

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:11.230
Indeed, that's true.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.820
But there is too little response from the instruments I set up.

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:18.370
There's been no heat signature or strange noises.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.480
Not even a hint of spectral activity.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:22.830
The data is completely within the normal range.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:26.000
Then what trapped the priestess?

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.880
What attacked me?!

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.340
What stopped the video, broke the glass, and moved the chair?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.090
That is why I said I'm still not convinced.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:38.340
Maybe it's a ghost that's powerful enough
to pretend that it's not there.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.310
What do you think, monk?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.190
As I've said from the beginning, it's the ghost of a suicide.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:48.770
And you, John?

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:50.730
I don't know.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.780
I agree with them, this is risky.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.940
And what about you?

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.700
I'll withhold my opinion for now.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.660
I'd like to investigate from a different angle.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.910
I wonder what he'll do. That kid...

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:10.580
He brings in all his fancy equipment,

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:12.130
and I wonder if it really does anything.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:15.630
Then, I think...

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.190
The exorcist finally makes his appearance.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.650
Our Father which art in Heaven,

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.650
Hallowed be thy name.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.070
What's that water?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:40.860
It's holy water.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.030
In the beginning was the Word,

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:46.790
And the Word was with God,

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.750
And the Word was God.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:54.920
What?

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:56.590
Isn't that more ghostly sounds?

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.380
Turn up the volume.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:02.550
The same was in the beginning with God.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.510
All things were made through Him.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:09.430
And without Him was not anything made that was made.

00:11:10.850 --> 00:11:14.230
In Him was life; and the life was the light of men.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.190
And the light shineth in darkness;

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.940
and the darkness comprehended it not.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:23.140
There was a man sent from God, whose name was John.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.120
The roof...

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:24.740
The same came or a witness...

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:28.910
But as many as received him,

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:29.900
Hey... girl!

00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:30.580
Bad!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:31.710
This is bad!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.250
To them gave he power to become the sons of God,

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:38.010
They, not through earth...

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:38.880
John!

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:39.840
Mai-san?

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:41.130
Hurry!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.510
The roof's coming down!

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:44.640
John!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.020
John!

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.860
My goodness...

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:57.900
If Mai-san hadn't called out to me,

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.070
it would have been very bad,

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.360
Perhaps we should stay away from here tonight.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:04.740
Mai, you may go.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:05.870
Really?

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:06.740
Yes.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.120
I think I'll be going as well.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.500
Gotta get some sleep.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.920
Honestly, you mean you're scared.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.010
I think I'll take your advice too

00:12:24.010 --> 00:12:26.430
and head home.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:27.850
And you, Naru?

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.180
There's something I still want to check out.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.980
But what if the roof caves in again?

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:53.460
Naru!

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.870
You slept here?

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.000
You'll catch cold.

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:00.380
Mai?

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.710
What are you doing here, so early in the morning?

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.180
D-Dammit,

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:10.430
he's really handsome.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.560
Morning?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.560
It's past eleven already!

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.390
Hey!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:17.850
What happened, scientist?

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.900
You getting ready to leave, kid?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.190
Indeed.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:25.570
It's out of your league, so you're just gonna run?

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:26.570
Oh, no...

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:27.820
No.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:30.410
I've determined that this incident is solved.

00:13:30.990 --> 00:13:33.410
You exorcised that whole place on your own?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.580
No, I didn't, and there was no need.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.920
What do you mean...?

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.000
What do you mean?

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:44.630
I took some readings last night.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.470
This is a seismograph.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:52.600
The old school building sank 0.2 inches last night.

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:53.600
What?!

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.640
It's a ground subsidence.

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.230
Then...

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.770
You mean all of this was because of this subsidence?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:04.150
I assumed that this place was reclaimed from a swamp.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.900
When I examined the distribution of
water wells once used in the area,

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:11.370
I established the existence of a large
aquifer running right under the school,

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:15.620
so I checked the wells nearby. They've all dried up.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:16.870
And that means?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:20.750
If the aquifer dries up and the land subsides,

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:22.460
it leaves a cavity underground,

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.460
which naturally, will affect any buildings up above.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.470
Then...

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:32.470
the chair moving and the roof collapsing
were all because of this subsidence?

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:33.390
Yes.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.230
The classroom on the east side, where the roof
collapsed, was three inches below the west side.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.020
Three inches, huh?

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.320
About sevenand a half centimetres then.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.530
Then what about those ghostly noises?

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.030
It was the sound of the building weakening.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:52.160
I think it would be best to declare this building off-limits.

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:56.540
This building will collapse soon.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.460
No way!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.540
Then what attacked me?!

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.050
If that did indeed happen,

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.680
perhaps it was a ghost that follows you around.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.050
It's true!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.180
I was really attacked!

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.100
Are you really leaving, Naru?

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.690
Yes, my work is done.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:21.600
I see.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:23.980
That is true...

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:29.690
Hmm, I just feel something is missing.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:34.200
There really is a ghost.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:35.700
There isn't.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.790
The results of my investigation were completely negative.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.210
You just might not know it!

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.830
Then you should exorcise it.

00:15:44.500 --> 00:15:46.130
If you do indeed possess such powers.

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.550
I feel that my work here is done, so I'm leaving. That's all.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:02.230
It's like my dream is gone...

00:16:03.310 --> 00:16:08.110
There's always these old buildings in schools,

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.240
and ghost stories about them...

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:13.660
It's kind of romantic, don't you think?

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.450
I don't like the idea of people dying,

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:20.160
but telling ghost stories is just harmless fun.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:21.830
Is that so?

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:30.710
Kuroda-san!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.140
What is this?

00:16:38.510 --> 00:16:39.560
Someone's knocking!

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:41.220
And it's really knockin'!

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.100
Another of the Tizzana criteria.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:44.100
Naru!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.310
Naru?

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.280
This is really bad!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:55.280
Get outside!

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:56.160
The building's collapsing!

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:57.240
Mai!

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:58.950
But the doors...!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:00.790
Leave that to me!

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:03.120
Get out this way!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.630
Are you all right, Kuroda-san?

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.210
You're bleeding. Hold out your hand.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.220
You'll be fine, the wound is very slight.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:17.050
What <i>was</i> that just now?

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:19.140
You saying that was a ground subsidence?

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.350
That was a poltergeist, well and proper!

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.770
That wasn't the sound of a collapsing building.

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.850
There was definitely something knocking on the walls!

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:32.940
This makes for four of Tizzana's nine criteria.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.280
What do you mean by negative results?

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.240
Ridiculous.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.200
We were nearly taken in by this kid's prank.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:45.040
Now we'll have to show you how the big boys do things.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.120
Good lord, I can't stand him!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:50.500
What was all that?

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.670
<i>Now</i> they get along?

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:56.300
Naru?

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:57.050
Your hand!

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:58.930
It's nothing, really.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:01.010
It'll scab over soon.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.010
But...

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:03.470
I'm fine.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.480
Look after Kuroda-san.

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:06.850
Naru!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:10.900
I'd like you to leave me alone for now.

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:14.030
I feel sick with self-loathing.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.500
Come to see the monk's exorcism?

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.380
No thanks.

00:18:35.710 --> 00:18:40.010
Want some help... cleanin' up?

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:42.970
I just have to take some stuff out.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:45.560
Then I'll take this for you.

00:18:46.140 --> 00:18:47.480
Can you wait a moment?

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.900
You still believe that kid's theory?

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.770
Do you have any evidence that he's wrong?

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:57.240
Prove to me that it was an evil spirit!

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.700
Now, now...

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:15.380
Is that nonsense chanting going to drive away evil spirits?

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.840
God, that darn Naru!

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:22.800
Come back and give 'em what for!

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:28.100
I set up yer mike on the second floor.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.270
Thanks.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.350
Sorry to make you help me...

00:19:31.770 --> 00:19:32.940
I don't mind.

00:19:33.350 --> 00:19:36.070
I'm gonna take a little look-see over there.

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:38.030
Sure, be careful.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:42.410
It's all well that I've decided to wait for Naru.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.820
But is he really coming back?

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.080
Naru?

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.210
Kuroda-san.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.540
How is it?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.170
Well, the monk and company are still looking around.

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:57.710
And Shibuya-san?

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:59.380
Off somewhere.

00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:02.630
Man, are there really any evil spirits here?

00:20:03.340 --> 00:20:04.510
I saw them.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:07.930
Yeah, you said that...

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:10.020
Well, they're not here any more.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.810
The exorcism was a success.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:15.310
You said that before and it failed!

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:17.110
It's fine this time!

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:18.270
They're still here.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:21.650
I can feel them.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.240
There are still many spirits here.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:25.870
Playing medium again?

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:29.240
Stop it. I'm the pro here.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:32.620
It would seem that isn't saying much.

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:34.290
It's all good.

00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:38.000
Ayako's one thing, but I did it this time.

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.420
What was that?!

00:20:39.420 --> 00:20:41.550
Just the truth.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:43.880
Trying to take credit for other people's work?

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.090
You too.

00:20:45.090 --> 00:20:46.340
Don't mock me!

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:48.180
Come on!

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:50.680
I hear something.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:53.770
There's someone there.

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:55.770
It can't be...

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:04.740
Monk!

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:10.490
Is someone there?

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:12.410
Nope.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:14.580
It must have been our imaginations.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.960
W-Wait... imaginations?

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.540
I heard it. Really!

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.340
You heard it too, right?

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.090
It was just the wind.

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:28.890
Admit it!

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:30.560
Your exorcism failed, didnt it?!

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:34.850
You were sniping at Naru's theory just a while ago,

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:37.650
but did he make some lame excuse about it?

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:41.070
You may be adults, but you're being childish!

00:21:41.360 --> 00:21:42.070
The knocking!

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.200
The footsteps have gotten faster!

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:49.570
There's a whole herd of 'em!

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.950
Hey! It's dangerous here,

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:52.990
Get out.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.160
R-Right!

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:54.790
Kuroda-san.

00:21:55.250 --> 00:21:56.000
Hurry!

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:05.340
Girlie!

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.840
Then I lost consciousness...

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:55.870
Filled with Evil Spirits?!

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:49.030
Next time: File 1 ~ Filled with Evil Spirits?! ~ #3.
